{
  "id": "Compound::DB00155 - Gene::353238",
  "verbalization": "L-citrulline is implicated in the regulation of Protein-arginine Deiminase Activity through its interaction with multiple Padi proteins, namely Padi1, Padi3, and Padi4. These proteins participate in the same biological process, which is central to the deamination of arginine residues. The shared involvement of these Padi proteins in the same activity suggests a functional link between L-citrulline and the overall regulation of this enzymatic pathway. The evidence from the three paths indicates that L-citrulline binds to different Padi proteins, which in turn participate in the same activity, ultimately leading to the involvement of Padi6. This suggests that Padi6 is a downstream component of the L-citrulline-mediated regulation of Protein-arginine Deiminase Activity. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of L-citrulline in modulating the activity of multiple Padi proteins, which may have implications for broader physiological processes involving arginine metabolism.",
